WEBVTT


00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:06.209
I just couldn't resist this
fun, colorful variegated yarn.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:10.110
It has short color repeats
and it was on sale.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.230
It will be perfect for
a Susanna's blanket.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:20.430
Now I experimented a bit and I found that
I liked tension six on my bulky machine,

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.140
so I made a swatch.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:22.980
It that tension.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:24.869
Okay.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:29.790
I know this is just a blanket, but without
a swatch, I can't be sure if I have enough

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:33.750
yarn or even what size to knit
with the yarn that I have.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.890
This is a 100% acrylic yarn, so I just
used a little bit of steam, detain the

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.310
curl, tame those edges to
make it easier to measure.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.150
I've knit a proper swatch.

00:00:48.675 --> 00:00:54.555
And measured between the yarn markers for
the stitches and between the marked rows

00:00:54.615 --> 00:00:56.115
for the rows.

00:00:56.865 --> 00:01:01.965
If you aren't familiar with knitting a
proper swatch, please visit the swatching

00:01:01.965 --> 00:01:06.395
classroom, knititnow.com/swatch.

00:01:07.245 --> 00:01:08.955
With my gauge established.

00:01:09.105 --> 00:01:12.765
I'll use my swatch and estimate
how much Yarn I'll need.

00:01:13.635 --> 00:01:16.725
I'll measure the entire
swatch from edge to edge.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.560
And I'll weigh it in grams.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:25.210
Armed with this info, I'm ready
to start building my pattern.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.160
Now, I'm not sure what size
blanket I'll be knitting.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:34.479
This is going to be for charity and it's
going to be based on how much yarn I have,

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.539
so I'll select bassinet size for now.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:43.860
Now notice that the pattern prompts you
with a standard size, but you can adjust

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:44.699
it if you like.

00:01:45.075 --> 00:01:46.965
And this might come in handy later.

00:01:48.585 --> 00:01:50.085
If you work in centimeters.

00:01:50.295 --> 00:01:51.915
Select centimeters here.

00:01:59.065 --> 00:02:02.125
I've entered my gauge in in four inches.

00:02:09.575 --> 00:02:12.755
I could put some notes in right
here for future reference.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:21.750
With the choices I've made, I"m generating
a pattern for a blanket that's 16 inches

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.970
wide and 36 inches long.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.110
Notice that I'm immediately prompted
to check if I have enough needles.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:34.570
Now, if I'm knitting a larger blanket, the
needle limitations of our needle bed might

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:35.740
come into play here.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.830
The green button, will
get the pattern started.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:47.450
This pop up again confirms my choices,
and in case you missed it, it confirms the

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:51.560
number of needles needed
for the width that I chose.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:56.570
Now, if I didn't have enough needles at
this point, I could go back and adjust the

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:57.200
width.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.670
Click the blue button,
and build the pattern.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.190
Now I'll come back to this page again.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:12.430
This is where I started and the details of
my custom pattern are listed right here.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:18.650
I'm still not sure what size, so
I'm going to use the yarn estimator.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:21.890
When I click the white yarn button,

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.950
I'll be prompted to
enter in my swatch data.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:36.120
I measured my width to be 7.5 inches
by 8.5 inches, and the swatch weighs 22

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:36.960
grams.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:42.540
Now for this small blanket,
I'll need about 198 grams.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:47.370
I have lots more yard than that, so
I'm going to try a different size.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:53.820
I'll start again, but this time I'll
select the next size up, which is a crib

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:54.690
size.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:58.800
I'll enter my gauge and the
details for the pattern.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:06.070
It's prompting me that I need 54 needles
this time, but still, no problem.

00:04:09.144 --> 00:04:14.834
When I come back to this page, notice the
new crib size pattern, my newest pattern

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:18.115
is at the top of the list
with all of its details.

00:04:20.185 --> 00:04:24.985
I'll click the yarn button to calculate
the yard based again on my swatch.

00:04:25.914 --> 00:04:30.445
And for this larger blanket,
I'm going to need 559 grams.

00:04:31.335 --> 00:04:37.034
If I want to make a change, I can either
choose a different size or modify the

00:04:37.034 --> 00:04:39.224
dimensions of the pattern that I built.

00:04:41.015 --> 00:04:43.685
The view button will display my pattern.

00:04:45.575 --> 00:04:49.234
This page repeats all the
details of my pattern.

00:04:49.895 --> 00:04:53.734
To get knitting, I'll
click blanket instructions.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:05:00.030
The Knit it NOw, pattern format is
designed to be viewed on an iPad or a

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.160
tablet, right at your knitting machine.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:06.870
You can watch the included videos
right from the pattern page.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:13.140
You can also hide and show the various
sections, making it easier to keep track

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:14.860
of where you are when you're knitting.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:19.969
If you prefer a printed
pattern, there are two options.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:25.219
Click the print button and you can print
the instructions as they're displayed on

00:05:25.219 --> 00:05:30.680
the screen, the videos and any detailed
instructions on the right hand side, they

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.480
won't clutter up the printed page.

00:05:32.659 --> 00:05:35.480
You'll be just printing
the knitting instructions.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:40.350
You also can choose to
download a PDF of the pattern.

00:05:49.695 --> 00:05:53.535
Again, the videos and detailed
instructions aren't included.

00:05:54.765 --> 00:05:55.695
Enough talk.

00:05:55.875 --> 00:05:57.565
I'm ready to get knitting.